#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:31
msgid "Chen Meilin"
msgstr "陈梅琳"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:32
msgid "Ceramicist"
msgstr "陶艺师"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:33
msgid "Jingdezhen, Jiangxi"
msgstr "江西景德镇"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:36
msgid "Porcelain thrown thin enough to hold the light."
msgstr "薄到足以承托光线的瓷器。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:38
msgid "Meilin trained for six years under a Jingdezhen master before opening a small studio on the eastern edge of the old kiln district. She works almost entirely in local porcelain stone, quarried an hour from her door."
msgstr "梅琳曾在景德镇一位陶艺大师门下学习六年，之后在古窑区东侧开设了一间小工作室。她几乎只使用本地瓷石，泥料取自离工作室一小时车程的地方。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:41
msgid "Her forms are quiet and slightly imperfect by design. A rim that dips a little, a foot left unglazed so you can read the clay -- these are the marks she leaves on purpose, and the reason no two pieces are alike."
msgstr "她的器形安静而略带不完美，这是刻意为之。微微下沉的器口、露出泥土质感的素烧足部，都是她有意留下的痕迹，也正是每件作品各不相同的原因。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:46
msgid "Clay is wedged by hand each morning and rested overnight before throwing."
msgstr "每天早晨手工揉泥，静置一夜后才开始拉坯。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:47
msgid "Every piece is turned on the wheel, then trimmed once leather-hard."
msgstr "每件作品都在转盘上完成，并在半干时修坯。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:48
msgid "Glazes are mixed in small batches from ash, feldspar and iron oxide."
msgstr "釉料以灰烬、长石和氧化铁分批调配。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:49
msgid "A single gas firing to 1280°C, with the kiln cooled slowly over two days."
msgstr "以 1280°C 进行一次燃气烧制，窑炉缓慢冷却两天。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:55
msgid "Lu Wenjing"
msgstr "陆文静"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:56
msgid "Weaver & natural dyer"
msgstr "织工与天然染色师"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:57
msgid "Dali, Yunnan"
msgstr "云南大理"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:60
msgid "Indigo that deepens with every wash."
msgstr "每一次清洗，靛蓝都更深一层。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:62
msgid "Wenjing learned to dye from her grandmother, who kept an indigo vat behind the family house in Dali. She now grows her own indigo and works with three neighbouring households during the harvest."
msgstr "文静向祖母学习染色。祖母曾在大理的家屋后经营一口靛蓝染缸。如今她自己种植蓝靛，并在收获季与邻近的三户人家合作。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:65
msgid "She weaves on a floor loom her father built, in cotton and hemp spun within the province. Nothing in her studio is dyed twice the same way, and she has stopped apologising for it."
msgstr "她使用父亲制作的木质地织机，以省内纺成的棉与麻织布。她工作室里的任何东西都不会以完全相同的方式染两次，她也不再为此道歉。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:70
msgid "Indigo is fermented in clay vats and fed weekly through the season."
msgstr "靛蓝在陶缸中发酵，并在整个季节每周补养。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:71
msgid "Cloth is dipped between six and fourteen times, depending on the depth wanted."
msgstr "布料浸染六至十四次，视所需深浅而定。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:72
msgid "Washed in river water and dried in shade to keep the colour even."
msgstr "在河水中清洗并于阴凉处晾干，使颜色保持均匀。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:73
msgid "Woven, finished and hemmed by hand on a wooden floor loom."
msgstr "在木质地织机上手工织造、整理与锁边。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:79
msgid "Zhao Hesheng"
msgstr "赵和生"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:80
msgid "Woodworker"
msgstr "木匠"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:81
msgid "Huizhou, Anhui"
msgstr "安徽徽州"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:84
msgid "Working with the grain, never against it."
msgstr "顺着木纹工作，从不与它对抗。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:86
msgid "Hesheng spent a decade restoring Huizhou timber houses before turning to smaller objects. He still sources most of his wood from those restorations -- beams and floorboards that have already lived a life."
msgstr "和生花了十年修复徽州木屋，之后才转向制作更小的器物。他的大部分木材仍来自这些修复工程，是已经度过一段岁月的梁木与地板。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:89
msgid "He cuts joinery by hand and finishes everything in raw linseed oil. Nothing leaves the bench until it feels right in the hand."
msgstr "他手工切削榫卯，所有作品都以生亚麻籽油完成。每件东西在握感恰到好处之前，都不会离开工作台。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:93
msgid "Reclaimed timber is milled, then rested for a season to settle."
msgstr "回收木材先加工，再静置一季让它稳定下来。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:94
msgid "Every joint is cut and pared by hand -- no dowels, no filler."
msgstr "每个榫接都手工切削与修整，不用木钉，也不用填料。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:95
msgid "Surfaces are worked through five grades of abrasive to a soft sheen."
msgstr "表面经过五种不同粗细的磨料处理，呈现柔和光泽。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:96
msgid "Finished in food-safe linseed oil, reapplied three times over a week."
msgstr "使用食品级亚麻籽油完成表面处理，一周内重复涂刷三次。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:102
msgid "Xu Anying"
msgstr "徐安莹"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:103
msgid "Candlemaker & perfumer"
msgstr "制烛师与调香师"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:104
msgid "Suzhou, Jiangsu"
msgstr "江苏苏州"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:107
msgid "Scent built the way a garden is planted."
msgstr "像栽种花园一样构筑香气。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:109
msgid "Anying studied classical Chinese garden design before training in perfumery. She thinks about a scent the way she was taught to think about a courtyard: what you meet first, and what you find later."
msgstr "安莹曾学习中国古典园林设计，之后接受调香训练。她以设计庭院的方式思考香气：首先遇见什么，之后又会发现什么。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:112
msgid "She pours in batches of forty, by hand, in a converted ground-floor workshop near the canal. Each batch is left to cure for two weeks before a wick is ever lit."
msgstr "她在运河附近一间改造的底层工作室里手工浇注，每批四十支。每批蜡烛会静置固化两周，之后才点燃烛芯。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:117
msgid "Essential oils are blended and left to marry for ten days."
msgstr "精油混合后静置十天，让香气彼此融合。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:118
msgid "Soy and rapeseed wax is melted low, never above 65°C."
msgstr "大豆蜡与菜籽蜡低温融化，温度不超过 65°C。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:119
msgid "Poured by hand in batches of forty, one vessel at a time."
msgstr "每次一只容器，分批手工浇注，每批四十支。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:120
msgid "Cured for fourteen days, then burn-tested from every batch."
msgstr "固化十四天后，从每批中抽样进行燃烧测试。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:126
msgid "Ye Ruolan"
msgstr "叶若兰"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:127
msgid "Textile artist"
msgstr "纺织艺术家"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:128
msgid "Hangzhou, Zhejiang"
msgstr "浙江杭州"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:131
msgid "Linen washed until it forgets it was ever stiff."
msgstr "将亚麻洗到仿佛从未僵硬过。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:133
msgid "Ruolan works in European flax linen, finished in her own studio using a stone-washing process she spent two years refining. The point, she says, is for a new piece to feel like one you have owned for years."
msgstr "若兰使用欧洲亚麻，在自己的工作室里以经过两年改良的石洗工艺完成整理。她说，理想状态是让新作品摸起来像已经陪伴你多年的旧物。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:136
msgid "She cuts and sews everything herself, with a single assistant during busy months, and keeps her ranges deliberately small."
msgstr "她亲自裁剪和缝制所有作品，忙碌月份会有一名助手，并始终刻意保持系列精简。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:140
msgid "Flax linen is sourced from a single mill and cut in small lays."
msgstr "亚麻来自同一家纺厂，并以小批量裁片处理。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:141
msgid "Seams are sewn, then the finished piece is stone-washed twice."
msgstr "缝合后，成品进行两次石洗。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:142
msgid "Dried flat and pressed once, lightly, to keep the natural crumple."
msgstr "平铺晾干后只轻轻熨烫一次，保留自然的褶皱。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\makers.py:143
msgid "Checked seam by seam before it is folded and wrapped."
msgstr "逐条检查缝线，再折叠包裹。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:18
msgid "Placing, changing and cancelling."
msgstr "下单、修改与取消。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:20
msgid "Can I change or cancel my order?"
msgstr "我可以修改或取消订单吗？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:21
msgid "Yes, within 12 hours of placing it, as long as it has not been packed. Email the studio with your order number and we will sort it out. After 12 hours a made-to-order piece may already be in production."
msgstr "可以。下单后 12 小时内，且订单尚未打包时，您可以修改或取消订单。请将订单编号发送至工作室邮箱，我们会为您处理。超过 12 小时后，按订单制作的商品可能已经开始生产。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:24
msgid "I ordered several pieces. Will they arrive together?"
msgstr "我订购了多件商品，它们会一起送达吗？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:25
msgid "Not always. In-stock items ship immediately and made-to-order pieces follow when they are ready. You are only charged delivery once."
msgstr "不一定。现货商品会立即发出，按订单制作的商品则会在完成后寄出。您只需支付一次配送费。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:27
msgid "Do you take custom or commission requests?"
msgstr "你们接受定制或委托制作吗？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:28
msgid "For some pieces, yes. Use the enquiry link on the product page and the maker will reply with what is possible and a quotation. Commissions typically take four to eight weeks."
msgstr "部分商品可以。请使用商品页面上的咨询链接，匠人会回复可行方案和报价。委托制作通常需要 4–8 周。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:31
msgid "Can I order a piece that is sold out?"
msgstr "我可以订购已售罄的商品吗？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:32
msgid "Sold-out pieces return when the maker next fires or weaves a batch. Add your email on the product page and you will hear when it does."
msgstr "已售罄的商品会在匠人下一次烧制或织造一批时重新上架。在商品页面留下您的电子邮箱，补货时我们会通知您。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:35
msgid "Timings, costs and tracking."
msgstr "时效、费用与物流查询。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:37
msgid "How long does delivery take?"
msgstr "配送需要多长时间？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:38
msgid "In-stock orders are dispatched in 2–4 working days and arrive within a week domestically. Made-to-order pieces state their own lead time on the product page."
msgstr "现货订单会在 2–4 个工作日内发出，并在一周内送达国内地址。按订单制作的商品会在商品页面注明各自的交付周期。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:40
msgid "How much does delivery cost?"
msgstr "配送费是多少？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:41
msgid "Standard delivery is ¥8. It is complimentary on orders above ¥80. Express delivery is ¥18 and dispatches the next working day where stock allows."
msgstr "标准配送费为 ¥8。订单金额超过 ¥80 可免配送费。加急配送费为 ¥18，并会在库存允许的情况下于下一个工作日发出。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:43
msgid "Do you ship internationally?"
msgstr "可以寄送到海外吗？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:44
msgid "Yes, to most countries. Duties and import taxes are not included and are paid by the recipient on arrival."
msgstr "可以，我们可寄送至大多数国家。关税和进口税不包含在费用中，需由收件人在收货时支付。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:46
msgid "How is fragile work packed?"
msgstr "易碎作品如何包装？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:47
msgid "Ceramics are wrapped in recycled tissue and moulded pulp, inside a double-walled box. No plastic, no polystyrene."
msgstr "陶瓷会用再生薄纸和模塑纸浆包裹，再装入双层瓦楞纸箱。全程不使用塑料或聚苯乙烯泡沫。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:50
msgid "Changing your mind, and breakages."
msgstr "改变主意与收到破损商品。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:52
msgid "What is your returns window?"
msgstr "退货期限是多久？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:53
msgid "Thirty days from delivery, for unused pieces in their original packaging. Tell us before you send anything back so we can issue a return reference."
msgstr "自收货之日起 30 天内，未使用且保留原包装的商品可以退货。寄回任何商品前请先联系我们，以便我们提供退货编号。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:55
msgid "Something arrived broken."
msgstr "收到的商品破损了。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:56
msgid "Send a photograph within 48 hours of delivery and we will replace it or refund you in full. You do not need to return the damaged piece."
msgstr "请在收货后 48 小时内发送照片，我们会为您更换商品或全额退款。您无需寄回破损商品。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:58
msgid "Can I return a made-to-order or commissioned piece?"
msgstr "按订单制作或委托制作的商品可以退货吗？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:59
msgid "Only if it is faulty. These are made specifically for you, so we cannot resell them. The product page says clearly when this applies."
msgstr "只有商品存在瑕疵时才可以。这些商品是专门为您制作的，无法再次销售。适用此规则时，商品页面会明确说明。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:61
msgid "Who pays return postage?"
msgstr "退货邮费由谁承担？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:62
msgid "We do, if the piece is faulty or not what you ordered. For a change of mind, return postage is yours."
msgstr "如果商品有瑕疵或与您订购的不符，退货邮费由我们承担。如果只是改变主意，退货邮费由您承担。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:65
msgid "Product Care"
msgstr "作品保养"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:65
msgid "Keeping pieces well for years."
msgstr "让作品长久保持良好状态。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:67
msgid "Is your stoneware dishwasher safe?"
msgstr "炻器可以用洗碗机清洗吗？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:68
msgid "Yes. It is fired to full vitrification. Hand washing keeps a matte glaze looking its best for longer, but the machine will not harm it."
msgstr "可以。炻器已经烧至完全玻化。手洗能让哑光釉面更长久地保持最佳状态，但洗碗机不会损坏它。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:70
msgid "How should I wash linen?"
msgstr "亚麻制品应该如何清洗？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:71
msgid "Cool machine wash on a gentle cycle, mild detergent, no fabric softener. Line dry in shade. It softens with every wash."
msgstr "使用温和洗涤剂，以低温轻柔模式机洗，不要使用衣物柔顺剂。置于阴凉处晾干。每洗一次，它都会更加柔软。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:73
msgid "My candle is tunnelling."
msgstr "我的蜡烛出现了隧道现象。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:74
msgid "Let the first burn run until the melt pool reaches the edge -- usually two to three hours. Wax has a memory, and the first burn sets it."
msgstr "第一次燃烧时，请让融蜡池延伸到容器边缘，通常需要两到三个小时。蜡具有记忆效应，第一次燃烧会决定之后的燃烧方式。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:76
msgid "The brass has darkened."
msgstr "黄铜变暗了。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:77
msgid "It is unlacquered, so that is expected and reversible. A little lemon juice and bicarbonate returns the shine if you want it back."
msgstr "黄铜没有上漆，因此变暗属于正常现象，也可以恢复。如果想让它重新亮起来，可使用少量柠檬汁和小苏打。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:80
msgid "Handmade Variations"
msgstr "手作差异"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:81
msgid "What is a variation, and what is a fault."
msgstr "什么是正常差异，什么属于瑕疵。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:83
msgid "My piece does not look exactly like the photograph."
msgstr "我的商品看起来与照片不完全一样。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:84
msgid "It will not. Glaze colour, speckle, and dye depth vary between firings and dye baths. We photograph a typical piece rather than the best one in a batch."
msgstr "本来就不会完全一样。不同批次的烧制和染浴会造成釉色、斑点和染色深浅的差异。我们拍摄的是具有代表性的作品，而不是一批中最好的一件。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:86
msgid "Are the dimensions exact?"
msgstr "尺寸是完全准确的吗？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:87
msgid "Within about 5%. Every piece is thrown or cut by hand, and clay shrinks by roughly a tenth in the firing."
msgstr "误差约在 5% 以内。每件作品都由手工拉坯或裁切，陶土在烧制过程中还会收缩约十分之一。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:89
msgid "There are fine lines in the glaze."
msgstr "釉面上有细纹。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:90
msgid "That is crazing, and on a vitrified body it is cosmetic. It does not affect strength or whether the piece holds water."
msgstr "这是开片。对于已经玻化的坯体，这只是外观上的变化，不会影响强度或盛水性能。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:92
msgid "What actually counts as a fault?"
msgstr "什么情况才算瑕疵？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:93
msgid "A chip, a crack through the body, a piece that does not sit flat, or a seam that has failed. Any of those, tell us and we will replace it."
msgstr "崩口、贯穿坯体的裂纹、无法平稳放置，或接缝开裂，都属于瑕疵。遇到任何一种情况，请告诉我们，我们会为您更换。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:96
msgid "Gifting"
msgstr "礼赠"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:96
msgid "Notes, wrapping and gift orders."
msgstr "留言、包装与礼品订单。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:98
msgid "Can you include a handwritten note?"
msgstr "可以附上手写留言吗？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:99
msgid "Yes. Add your message at checkout and it is written onto a card by hand, unsigned by us, and tucked into the parcel."
msgstr "可以。结账时填写留言，我们会将其手写在卡片上，不署工作室名，并放入包裹中。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:101
msgid "Will the recipient see the price?"
msgstr "收件人会看到价格吗？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:102
msgid "No. Parcels never contain an invoice. Pricing is emailed to you only."
msgstr "不会。包裹中绝不会放入发票。价格信息只会通过电子邮件发送给您。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:103
msgid "Is gift wrapping extra?"
msgstr "礼品包装需要额外收费吗？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:104
msgid "No. Everything is wrapped in unbleached paper and cotton string as standard. There is nothing extra to add."
msgstr "不需要。所有商品都会按标准使用未漂白纸张和棉绳包装，无需另行添加。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:106
msgid "Do you sell gift cards?"
msgstr "你们销售礼品卡吗？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\faqs.py:107
msgid "Yes, in ¥50, ¥100 and ¥200. They are emailed to the recipient on a date you choose and do not expire."
msgstr "有 ¥50、¥100 和 ¥200 三种面额。礼品卡会在您选择的日期通过电子邮件发送给收件人，且不会过期。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Why no two glazes match"
msgstr "为什么没有两种釉色完全相同"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "A wood-ash glaze is a record of the firing that made it. Here is why we stopped trying to make them identical."
msgstr "手工灰釉记录着烧制它的过程。我们为什么不再追求完全一致？"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Craft"
msgstr "工艺"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "6 min"
msgstr "6 分钟"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Ask a factory to make five hundred mugs the same colour and it will. Ask a kiln to do it and you will get something more interesting and less obedient."
msgstr "让工厂把五百只马克杯做成同一种颜色，它可以做到。让窑炉这样做，你得到的会是更有意思、也更不听话的东西。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "What the kiln decides"
msgstr "窑炉的决定"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Ash glaze is mixed from what is swept out of the kiln after a firing -- wood ash, feldspar, a little iron oxide, water. The proportions are consistent. What is not consistent is where a piece sits in the kiln, how the flame moves around it, and how fast that corner cools over the two days afterwards."
msgstr "灰釉由每次烧制后从窑炉中清扫出的材料调配而成——木灰、长石、少量氧化铁和水。配比始终一致。无法保持一致的是器物在窑中的位置、火焰绕过它的方式，以及之后两天里那个角落冷却的速度。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "A mug on the top shelf near the flue will come out a shade greener than the same mug, from the same batch of glaze, on the bottom shelf. Neither is the correct one."
msgstr "靠近烟道的上层窑架上，一只马克杯出窑时会比下层窑架上那只使用同批釉料的同款杯子更偏绿一些。两者都不是唯一正确的样子。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "We fire to a range, not a number. The kiln finishes the piece, and it does not take instruction."
msgstr "我们烧制的是一个范围，而不是一个数字。器物由窑炉完成，它不听从指令。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Living with variation"
msgstr "与差异共处"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "This has a practical consequence for anyone buying a set. If you order four bowls, you will get four bowls that clearly belong together and are clearly not identical. Over a few years of use they diverge further -- the ones you reach for most develop a slightly different surface."
msgstr "这会给购买成套器物的人带来一个实际结果。如果你订购四只碗，收到的四只显然属于一套，也显然并不完全相同。使用几年后，它们之间的差异还会加深——你最常拿取的那些，表面会逐渐呈现稍有不同的状态。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "We used to photograph the most even piece of a batch. We now photograph a middling one, because it is closer to what arrives."
msgstr "过去，我们会拍摄一批中最均匀的那一件。现在，我们拍摄处于中间状态的一件，因为它更接近你实际收到的样子。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "An indigo vat in Dali"
msgstr "大理的一口靛蓝染缸"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Lu Wenjing keeps four fermenting vats behind her house. Feeding them is a weekly job that has no shortcut."
msgstr "陆文静在家后院养着四口发酵染缸，每周照料，没有捷径。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "8 min"
msgstr "8 分钟"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "The vats are clay, sunk to the rim in the ground behind the house, and they are alive in a fairly literal sense. Indigo does not dissolve in water. It has to be reduced by bacteria first, and those bacteria need feeding, warmth and time."
msgstr "这些染缸由陶土制成，埋在屋后的地里，缸口与地面齐平；从相当直观的意义上说，它们是活的。靛蓝不溶于水，必须先由细菌还原，而这些细菌需要养料、温度和时间。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "A weekly rhythm"
msgstr "每周的节奏"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Every Monday Wenjing adds wheat bran and lime, stirs each vat and checks the surface for the coppery film that says the vat is working. A healthy vat smells sweet. An unhappy one smells of nothing at all, which is worse."
msgstr "每逢星期一，文静都会加入麦麸和石灰，搅动每口染缸，并查看表面是否出现说明染缸运作正常的铜色薄膜。健康的染缸带着甜香；状态不佳的染缸则什么气味也没有，而这更糟。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Cloth goes in yellow-green and turns blue in the air, in front of you, over about twenty seconds. Six dips gives a pale sky. Fourteen gives the near-black indigo on our heaviest throws."
msgstr "布料入缸时呈黄绿色，在你眼前接触空气后变成蓝色，整个过程约二十秒。浸染六次会得到浅淡的天蓝色；十四次则会得到我们最厚重盖毯上近乎黑色的靛蓝。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Why it fades the way it does"
msgstr "为什么会这样褪色"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Indigo sits on the outside of the fibre rather than inside it. That is why indigo cloth wears at the folds and the edges first, and why a piece you use every week will look different from one kept in a cupboard. It is also why it will never look worse -- only more specific to you."
msgstr "靛蓝附着在纤维外部，而非进入纤维内部。因此靛蓝织物会先在折叠处和边缘磨损，每周使用的织物也会与一直收在柜中的那件呈现不同面貌。也正因如此，它永远不会变得更糟——只会越来越带有属于你的痕迹。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "How to care for handmade ceramics"
msgstr "如何保养手作陶器"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Most of what shortens the life of a handmade piece is heat, not use."
msgstr "真正缩短手作器物寿命的，多数是高温，而不是日常使用。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "4 min"
msgstr "4 分钟"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Our stoneware is fired high enough to be fully vitrified, which means it is dishwasher safe and will not absorb water or odours. You can put it in the machine without thinking about it."
msgstr "我们的炻器以足够高的温度烧至完全玻化，这意味着它可以放入洗碗机，也不会吸收水分或气味。放进机器清洗时，无需多虑。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "The thing that will actually damage a piece is thermal shock -- a hot bowl into cold water, or a cold plate into a hot oven. Glaze and clay expand at slightly different rates, and a sharp change can craze the surface or, occasionally, crack the piece outright. Let things cool first."
msgstr "真正会损坏器物的是热震——把热碗放入冷水，或把冷盘放进热烤箱。釉料与陶土的膨胀速度略有不同，温度骤变可能使釉面产生开片，偶尔甚至会让器物彻底开裂。先让它们冷却。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Unglazed feet will pick up marks from the table over time. That is normal and, in our view, an improvement. If it bothers you, a light rub with a damp cloth and a little bicarbonate lifts most of it."
msgstr "未施釉的圈足会随时间从桌面沾上痕迹。这很正常，在我们看来反而更好看。如果你介意，用湿布蘸少量小苏打轻轻擦拭，就能去除大部分痕迹。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Fine crazing -- a web of hairline lines in the glaze -- is not a crack and does not affect whether a piece holds water. In a vitrified body it is cosmetic."
msgstr "细密的开片——釉面上如网状分布的发丝纹——并不是裂缝，也不影响器物盛水。对于已经玻化的坯体，它只是外观上的变化。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "The case for buying less"
msgstr "少买一些的理由"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "We make about four hundred pieces a month. Here is why we have no plans to make four thousand."
msgstr "我们每月制作约四百件作品，这就是不打算制作四千件的原因。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "7 min"
msgstr "7 分钟"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Every year we are asked why we do not scale. The honest answer is that the thing people like about the work is a direct consequence of how little of it there is."
msgstr "每年都有人问我们为什么不扩大规模。坦率地说，人们喜欢这些作品，正是因为它们数量有限。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "A studio making four hundred pieces a month can afford to lose a firing. It can let a maker spend a season on a shape that may not sell. It can turn down the wholesale order that would have paid for a second kiln but required the glaze to be standardised first."
msgstr "一家每月制作四百件作品的工作室，经得起一次烧制失败。它可以让匠人用一整个季节琢磨一种未必卖得出去的器形；也可以拒绝一笔本可支付第二座窑炉费用、却要求先把釉色标准化的批发订单。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "None of that survives contact with volume. The pieces would still be competent. They would stop being specific."
msgstr "一旦产量扩大，这些都无法维持。器物依然会做得合格，却不再具有鲜明的个性。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "This has a cost, and we would rather be plain about it: some things sell out and do not come back for months, and made-to-order items really do take three weeks. We think that is the better trade."
msgstr "这会带来代价，我们愿意坦白说明：有些作品售罄后要几个月才会回来，按订单制作的商品也确实需要三周。我们认为，这样的取舍更好。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "A table set for nothing in particular"
msgstr "一张没有特别理由的餐桌"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Notes on using the good plates on a Tuesday."
msgstr "在星期二也用上那些好盘子。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Interiors"
msgstr "室内"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "5 min"
msgstr "5 分钟"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "There is a particular cupboard, in a lot of houses, where the good things live. They come out twice a year and spend the rest of their life being protected from the very thing they were made for."
msgstr "许多家里都有一个专门的柜子，里面放着那些好东西。它们一年只拿出来两次，其余时间都被保护着，远离它们原本被制作出来要服务的用途。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Handmade pieces are, counter-intuitively, better suited to daily use than to occasional display. They are not delicate. High-fired stoneware is tougher than most factory porcelain, and washed linen is at its best after fifty washes rather than five."
msgstr "有些反直觉的是，手工作品比起偶尔陈列，其实更适合日常使用。它们并不娇贵。高温烧制的炻器比大多数工厂瓷器更坚实，水洗亚麻也要洗过五十次，而不是五次，才会呈现最好的状态。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "The argument for using them is not really about the objects. It is that a weeknight dinner eaten off something someone made by hand is a different kind of evening, at no additional cost, on a day that had nothing else to recommend it."
msgstr "使用它们的理由，其实不只关乎物件本身。在一个原本平淡无奇的工作日里，用某个人亲手制作的器皿吃一顿晚餐，不需增加任何花费，却会让那个夜晚变得不同。"

#: .\frontend\mockdata\journal.py
msgid "Our suggestion is unglamorous: take the good plates out of the high cupboard and put them where the everyday ones are. Within a month you will stop noticing, which is the point."
msgstr "我们的建议并不华丽：把好盘子从高处的柜子里拿出来，放到日常餐具的位置。一个月内，你就不会再特意注意它们，而这正是意义所在。"

